1
00:00:25,926 --> 00:00:28,126
♪ ♪

2
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:38,303
♪ ♪

3
00:00:49,383 --> 00:00:51,450
♪ ♪

4
00:01:21,448 --> 00:01:24,382
♪ ♪

5
00:01:54,448 --> 00:01:57,382
♪ ♪

6
00:02:47,133 --> 00:02:50,068
♪ ♪

7
00:03:02,449 --> 00:03:03,582
♪ ♪

8
00:03:25,205 --> 00:03:27,472
Now, here's the
heart of it, Ben.

9
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:29,975
If I leave my Rudy
Vallée records

10
00:03:30,043 --> 00:03:32,610
to my sweet niece Charlene,

11
00:03:32,679 --> 00:03:35,113
then I've got to leave
my Nelson Eddy records

12
00:03:35,181 --> 00:03:36,948
to her whiny sister.

13
00:03:37,016 --> 00:03:38,150
Hmm.

14
00:03:38,218 --> 00:03:40,652
Those records
are priceless, Ben.

15
00:03:40,721 --> 00:03:41,787
Yeah.

16
00:03:41,855 --> 00:03:43,655
You're not taking notes.

17
00:03:43,724 --> 00:03:45,924
It's like I told you.

18
00:03:45,993 --> 00:03:48,459
There are wills you
can make out yourself

19
00:03:48,528 --> 00:03:50,573
where you don't have
to pay a person like me.

20
00:03:50,597 --> 00:03:53,131
Well, you know what they say.

21
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:56,701
A man who does his own
will has a fool for a will maker.

22
00:03:56,770 --> 00:03:58,937
That's not the saying. It's not?

23
00:03:59,006 --> 00:04:00,272
No, it's:

24
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:03,808
"A man who defends himself
has a fool for a lawyer."

25
00:04:03,877 --> 00:04:05,043
Mm, same thing.

26
00:04:06,714 --> 00:04:08,958
I'll tell you what,
tell you what.

27
00:04:08,982 --> 00:04:12,917
You make out a list and
I'll make sure it's legal.

28
00:04:12,986 --> 00:04:14,753
Ben, you're a genius.

29
00:04:14,821 --> 00:04:18,490
I'll be back with a list as
long as an encyclopedia.

30
00:04:21,027 --> 00:04:22,127
Oh, Mr. Matlock.

31
00:04:22,196 --> 00:04:24,196
Oh, please, you've
got to help me.

32
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:27,198
Mr. Matlock, my
name is Jennifer Holtz.

33
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:28,633
I'm a psychic.

34
00:04:28,702 --> 00:04:30,535
I can see into the future.

35
00:04:30,604 --> 00:04:33,938
Mr. Matlock, someone
is going to be murdered.

36
00:04:34,007 --> 00:04:35,807
It's not me, is it?

37
00:04:35,876 --> 00:04:38,010
What? It's not me.

38
00:04:38,078 --> 00:04:40,378
No, you're too small.

39
00:04:40,447 --> 00:04:41,913
Oh, good.

40
00:04:41,982 --> 00:04:42,982
Now, don't you worry.

41
00:04:43,050 --> 00:04:44,382
You come right with me

42
00:04:44,451 --> 00:04:46,751
and have a seat right in there,

43
00:04:46,820 --> 00:04:49,921
and everything's
going to be all right.

44
00:04:49,990 --> 00:04:53,325
Cute chick, but two
sandwiches short of a picnic,

45
00:04:53,393 --> 00:04:54,692
if you get my drift.

46
00:04:54,761 --> 00:04:56,294
Mm-hmm.

47
00:04:57,730 --> 00:05:02,233
Now, tell me, Miss Holtz,
what can we do to help you?

48
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:04,836
Well, I'm staying at
the Crown Regent Hotel

49
00:05:04,904 --> 00:05:06,605
for the New World convention.

50
00:05:06,674 --> 00:05:09,975
Oh, it's a gathering of
psychics and New Age people.

51
00:05:10,044 --> 00:05:11,609
It happened in my hotel room.

52
00:05:11,679 --> 00:05:15,580
Somebody was killed
in your hotel room?

53
00:05:15,649 --> 00:05:17,749
No, no, that's where
I had the vision.

54
00:05:19,319 --> 00:05:21,052
Oh, you must believe me.

55
00:05:21,121 --> 00:05:23,254
I saw it all.

56
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:26,924
A man... a tall, muscular man...

57
00:05:26,993 --> 00:05:29,127
Stabbed in the back
with a glass spear.

58
00:05:29,196 --> 00:05:31,262
Holy cow.

59
00:05:31,332 --> 00:05:34,210
Uh... let me, let me,
let me get this straight.

60
00:05:34,234 --> 00:05:37,468
Um, nobody's been killed?

61
00:05:38,571 --> 00:05:41,239
Within 48 hours,
this man will die,

62
00:05:41,307 --> 00:05:44,008
and I will be accused
of the murder.

63
00:05:44,077 --> 00:05:45,443
And I didn't do it.

64
00:05:45,512 --> 00:05:46,878
Of course you didn't.

65
00:05:46,947 --> 00:05:48,758
Well, no, she didn't because

66
00:05:48,782 --> 00:05:51,083
a murder hasn't been committed.

67
00:05:51,151 --> 00:05:53,985
What exactly is it that
you want, Miss Holtz?

68
00:05:54,054 --> 00:05:56,187
I need a defense lawyer.

69
00:05:56,256 --> 00:06:00,525
Well, you, you can't
be defended, uh,

70
00:06:00,594 --> 00:06:03,294
for murder until a
murder's been committed.

71
00:06:03,363 --> 00:06:04,730
I mean, somebody has to be dead.

72
00:06:04,798 --> 00:06:05,930
That's the law.

73
00:06:05,999 --> 00:06:08,266
You must help me,
please, Mr. Matlock.

74
00:06:08,334 --> 00:06:09,912
Maybe we'd bett-better
get something straight.

75
00:06:09,936 --> 00:06:12,003
<i>I'm</i> Mr. Matlock.

76
00:06:12,072 --> 00:06:14,772
He's Mr. Calhoun.

77
00:06:14,841 --> 00:06:17,008
I'm a retired businessman.

78
00:06:17,076 --> 00:06:18,088
You can call me Ace.

79
00:06:18,112 --> 00:06:20,111
You made a lot of money.

80
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:22,013
I've done pretty well.

81
00:06:22,082 --> 00:06:23,648
And will continue to do so.

82
00:06:23,717 --> 00:06:26,117
Really?

83
00:07:03,957 --> 00:07:05,234
Where's Jennifer Holtz?

84
00:07:05,258 --> 00:07:06,424
How would I know?

85
00:07:06,493 --> 00:07:07,704
Cyril's gone and
booked her a radio spot,

86
00:07:07,728 --> 00:07:09,238
and she's an hour late.

87
00:07:09,262 --> 00:07:10,973
Well, perhaps in the future
she sees, there aren't any clocks.

88
00:07:10,997 --> 00:07:12,630
Shh.

89
00:07:12,699 --> 00:07:14,677
We'd like you WZF
listeners to know this is

90
00:07:14,701 --> 00:07:16,867
the largest gathering
of psychics, healers,

91
00:07:16,936 --> 00:07:19,437
trance channelers ever
assembled in your city,

92
00:07:19,506 --> 00:07:20,950
and Jennifer Holtz
will appear daily.

93
00:07:20,974 --> 00:07:24,943
I was a headline channeler
before Jennifer Holtz

94
00:07:25,011 --> 00:07:27,244
knew her astral
projection from her karma.

95
00:07:27,313 --> 00:07:30,615
Second billing is an insult to
my spiritual entity Ramutiki.

96
00:07:30,684 --> 00:07:32,995
If Ramutiki survived
being beheaded in Babylon,

97
00:07:33,019 --> 00:07:35,364
I think he'll survive
second billing.

98
00:07:35,388 --> 00:07:38,122
Where do they get this garbage?

99
00:07:38,191 --> 00:07:39,491
They make it up.

100
00:07:39,559 --> 00:07:42,360
Ramutiki is predicting
an expanding economy,

101
00:07:42,429 --> 00:07:43,862
worldwide prosperity.

102
00:07:43,930 --> 00:07:45,763
Yes, there will be over
a hundred booths...

103
00:07:45,832 --> 00:07:48,833
Crystals, tarot readings,
aura readings, astrology,

104
00:07:48,902 --> 00:07:50,301
psychic healing, numerology,

105
00:07:50,370 --> 00:07:54,672
every aspect of
New Age thinking.

106
00:07:54,741 --> 00:07:59,010
Thank you, Mr. Fessman.

107
00:07:59,079 --> 00:08:02,213
Your Ramutiki is
off his astral nut.

108
00:08:02,282 --> 00:08:03,647
Saturn has gone into Capricorn;

109
00:08:03,716 --> 00:08:05,627
Wall Street's
heading for a crash.

110
00:08:05,651 --> 00:08:07,652
You're crazy.

111
00:08:07,721 --> 00:08:09,821
Uranus is in Capricorn
in the tenth house.

112
00:08:09,889 --> 00:08:11,589
The stock market will boom.

113
00:08:11,658 --> 00:08:13,491
Ramutiki told you this?

114
00:08:13,559 --> 00:08:15,071
I channeled him this
morning. Yeah, well,

115
00:08:15,095 --> 00:08:16,561
he's coming through fuzzy.

116
00:08:16,630 --> 00:08:18,796
Jennifer says
that... Jennifer again.

117
00:08:18,866 --> 00:08:20,232
Predicting a depression?

118
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:22,545
Oh, shut up, Spaulding.

119
00:08:22,569 --> 00:08:24,635
Has, uh, has anyone
seen Jennifer?

120
00:08:25,873 --> 00:08:27,438
Marie.

121
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:29,218
Jennifer, where have you been?

122
00:08:29,242 --> 00:08:31,354
Um, Jennifer, I could
use some advice.

123
00:08:31,378 --> 00:08:32,610
Of course.

124
00:08:32,679 --> 00:08:34,312
You look terrible.

125
00:08:34,381 --> 00:08:37,048
Haven't eaten or
slept, have you?

126
00:08:37,116 --> 00:08:39,116
Come on, we're
going to have lunch.

127
00:08:39,185 --> 00:08:40,418
We'll be back in an hour.

128
00:08:40,487 --> 00:08:41,563
Where are you going?

129
00:08:41,587 --> 00:08:42,520
You've got radio spots,

130
00:08:42,588 --> 00:08:43,800
you've got newspaper interviews.

131
00:08:43,824 --> 00:08:47,225
Well, this is important.

132
00:08:47,294 --> 00:08:51,796
Jennifer, you're the
best, and so beautiful.

133
00:08:51,865 --> 00:08:54,899
Oh, Dick.

134
00:08:54,968 --> 00:08:57,213
Why, how can you
be so cruel to her?

135
00:08:57,237 --> 00:08:59,170
Marie.

136
00:09:18,125 --> 00:09:22,393
Yeah, and then... then
she says... she says,

137
00:09:22,462 --> 00:09:26,264
"In 48 hours, a
man will be killed

138
00:09:26,332 --> 00:09:27,944
and I will be blamed
for the murder."

139
00:09:30,103 --> 00:09:32,236
♪ Doo-doo-doo-doo-doo-doo. ♪

140
00:09:32,305 --> 00:09:35,340
She was a nice
enough girl... attractive...

141
00:09:35,409 --> 00:09:36,753
Just one of those dames that's,

142
00:09:36,777 --> 00:09:39,110
you know, a bubble off plumb.

143
00:09:39,179 --> 00:09:40,545
As long as she was there,

144
00:09:40,614 --> 00:09:42,414
why didn't you ask her
to read your fortune?

145
00:09:42,482 --> 00:09:44,360
No, no, no, no fortune.

146
00:09:44,384 --> 00:09:45,594
I don't want to know
about the future.

147
00:09:45,618 --> 00:09:47,318
I want it to be
a surprise. Well,

148
00:09:47,387 --> 00:09:49,788
I just thought that you
might have asked her

149
00:09:49,856 --> 00:09:52,590
if there was anybody
special in your future.

150
00:09:52,659 --> 00:09:55,626
Oh, yeah, well...

151
00:09:58,465 --> 00:09:59,465
Here comes Les.

152
00:10:01,401 --> 00:10:03,401
Hey, Ben, you'll never guess.

153
00:10:03,470 --> 00:10:05,403
Oh, hi, Les.

154
00:10:05,472 --> 00:10:09,040
You know that high-tech
egg stock I told you about?

155
00:10:09,108 --> 00:10:12,877
Oh, Julie and I were just
having a, a quiet dinner.

156
00:10:12,946 --> 00:10:13,986
Well, go ahead, eat.

157
00:10:14,047 --> 00:10:16,513
Anyway, there was
a two-for-one split,

158
00:10:16,582 --> 00:10:19,184
and the stock went
right through the roof

159
00:10:19,252 --> 00:10:21,819
and I made a bundle,
just like she said.

160
00:10:21,888 --> 00:10:23,154
What are you talking about?

161
00:10:23,223 --> 00:10:24,556
Jennifer Holtz.

162
00:10:24,624 --> 00:10:27,725
She told me yesterday
I'd make a killing, and I did.

163
00:10:27,794 --> 00:10:30,895
And now she says my
hair is going to grow back.

164
00:10:30,964 --> 00:10:33,098
Oh, well, that's exciting.

165
00:10:35,134 --> 00:10:36,067
Hi, Julie. Hi.

166
00:10:36,136 --> 00:10:38,569
Boy, am I starved.

167
00:10:41,408 --> 00:10:43,252
How did you find
out we were here?

168
00:10:43,276 --> 00:10:45,443
Did Jennifer predict it?

169
00:10:45,512 --> 00:10:46,778
No.

170
00:10:46,847 --> 00:10:49,347
You think I'm some
sort of weirdo?

171
00:10:49,415 --> 00:10:52,083
I called your answering
service and they told me.

172
00:10:52,152 --> 00:10:53,084
Oh, hmm.

173
00:10:53,153 --> 00:10:54,819
Can I have your pickle?

174
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:10,268
Dick?

175
00:11:29,823 --> 00:11:32,056
Dick?

176
00:11:32,124 --> 00:11:34,859
Oh, my God!

177
00:11:34,928 --> 00:11:36,394
No!

178
00:11:36,463 --> 00:11:38,696
No... no!

179
00:11:41,334 --> 00:11:42,834
Hold it!

180
00:11:45,772 --> 00:11:47,516
I'm coming, I'm
coming, I'm coming.

181
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:48,773
I'm coming.

182
00:11:48,842 --> 00:11:50,374
Hold your horses.

183
00:11:50,443 --> 00:11:51,976
I'm coming.

184
00:11:52,045 --> 00:11:55,413
It happened, just as I saw it!

185
00:11:55,481 --> 00:11:56,959
What happened, Miss Holtz?

186
00:11:56,983 --> 00:12:00,618
The stabbing...
Just like my vision.

187
00:12:00,687 --> 00:12:03,488
Dick Blake... he's, he's dead.

188
00:12:03,557 --> 00:12:07,057
Stabbed in the back
with a crystal wand.

189
00:12:07,127 --> 00:12:08,593
Who's Dick Blake?

190
00:12:08,661 --> 00:12:11,729
He's the assistant
manager of the convention.

191
00:12:11,798 --> 00:12:14,765
I found him in
the Crystal Suite.

192
00:12:14,834 --> 00:12:17,168
Don't you see?

193
00:12:17,237 --> 00:12:19,370
It's just as I predicted.

194
00:12:19,439 --> 00:12:22,106
And now they're
going to accuse me.

195
00:12:22,175 --> 00:12:23,875
Oh.

196
00:12:23,944 --> 00:12:25,588
Wa-Was anybody else there?

197
00:12:25,612 --> 00:12:27,845
Well... no, when
I first went in,

198
00:12:27,914 --> 00:12:30,615
and... and then
someone came, and I...

199
00:12:30,684 --> 00:12:32,383
I panicked and ran.

200
00:12:32,452 --> 00:12:36,321
Oh. You ran from the
scene of the crime?

201
00:12:36,389 --> 00:12:37,855
Oh, I didn't kill him.

202
00:12:37,924 --> 00:12:39,969
Oh. Oh, you've got to help me.

203
00:12:39,993 --> 00:12:43,094
Oh. Well, we've got
to go to the police.

204
00:12:43,163 --> 00:12:45,396
Will you represent me?

205
00:12:45,465 --> 00:12:47,009
Oh, I knew you would.

206
00:12:47,033 --> 00:12:48,844
Oh, I don't know. I don't know.

207
00:12:48,868 --> 00:12:50,713
Uh, ah, sit down
somewhere. But...

208
00:12:50,737 --> 00:12:52,515
I've got to put on some pants

209
00:12:52,539 --> 00:12:54,472
if I'm going into town.

210
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:03,681
<i>Do you ever get the feeling</i>

211
00:13:03,750 --> 00:13:07,152
that people are-are...
are out to get you?

212
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:10,822
You're describing
paranoia, Mr. Matlock.

213
00:13:10,890 --> 00:13:12,423
And I'm not crazy.

214
00:13:12,491 --> 00:13:14,992
But you-you hear voices

215
00:13:15,061 --> 00:13:17,495
and-and-and spirits.

216
00:13:17,564 --> 00:13:18,696
Yes.

217
00:13:18,765 --> 00:13:20,765
I hear my guides
and my teachers.

218
00:13:20,834 --> 00:13:23,468
But not here.

219
00:13:23,536 --> 00:13:24,902
Here.

220
00:13:24,971 --> 00:13:29,607
Well, I don't... I
don't understand.

221
00:13:30,710 --> 00:13:32,610
Ever since I was a child,

222
00:13:32,678 --> 00:13:34,845
I... I had feelings.

223
00:13:34,914 --> 00:13:36,948
Intuitions about
what would happen.

224
00:13:38,618 --> 00:13:41,085
And then when I
learned to meditate,

225
00:13:41,153 --> 00:13:43,754
I started to have visions.

226
00:13:45,792 --> 00:13:48,359
For a while, I tried to deny it.

227
00:13:48,428 --> 00:13:52,396
I didn't want people to
think that I was crazy.

228
00:13:52,465 --> 00:13:55,800
So, I went to college,
got a real estate license.

229
00:13:56,970 --> 00:14:01,005
But... selling flats wasn't...

230
00:14:01,074 --> 00:14:04,275
I was put here to help
people, Mr. Matlock.

231
00:14:04,343 --> 00:14:06,277
Do you understand?

232
00:14:08,481 --> 00:14:10,515
Um...

233
00:14:10,584 --> 00:14:13,918
I don't understand
about being psychic.

234
00:14:15,689 --> 00:14:17,255
And I don't think

235
00:14:17,324 --> 00:14:19,624
the prosecution will
understand, either.

236
00:14:20,727 --> 00:14:22,738
I think he will understand

237
00:14:22,762 --> 00:14:26,697
a-a witness seeing you
flee the scene of a murder

238
00:14:26,766 --> 00:14:28,810
the day after you predicted it.

239
00:14:28,834 --> 00:14:31,568
What were you doing in
the Crystal Room that night?

240
00:14:34,173 --> 00:14:37,474
Dick asked me to
meet him at the office.

241
00:14:37,543 --> 00:14:39,243
I was giving him
private readings.

242
00:14:39,311 --> 00:14:42,981
He was in a very negative space.

243
00:14:43,049 --> 00:14:45,817
He seemed... almost desperate.

244
00:14:47,420 --> 00:14:49,987
When I got to the
office, he wasn't there,

245
00:14:50,056 --> 00:14:54,391
but I noticed the door to
the Crystal Suite was open.

246
00:14:54,460 --> 00:14:56,193
And that's where I found him.

247
00:14:59,632 --> 00:15:01,866
Well, w-why did you run?

248
00:15:01,934 --> 00:15:04,113
I mean, why didn't
you go for help?

249
00:15:04,137 --> 00:15:06,070
When I found Dick,

250
00:15:06,139 --> 00:15:08,306
the most horrifying
vision I've ever had

251
00:15:08,375 --> 00:15:10,608
in my life came true
in front of my eyes.

252
00:15:10,676 --> 00:15:13,111
I was afraid!

253
00:15:14,847 --> 00:15:16,514
Mm.

254
00:15:20,586 --> 00:15:21,818
I want my money!

255
00:15:21,887 --> 00:15:24,033
Spaulding, I've got much
bigger things to worry about

256
00:15:24,057 --> 00:15:25,389
than your paycheck.

257
00:15:25,458 --> 00:15:27,558
You'll have to wait
for your money.

258
00:15:27,627 --> 00:15:28,938
I don't have a cent.

259
00:15:28,962 --> 00:15:30,239
Why don't you
channel up Ramutiki

260
00:15:30,263 --> 00:15:32,129
and hit him up for a loan?

261
00:15:33,532 --> 00:15:36,100
Uh, excuse us. We're
looking for Iris Vogel.

262
00:15:36,169 --> 00:15:37,312
We're attorneys.

263
00:15:37,336 --> 00:15:39,081
I'm Michelle Thomas,
this is Ben Matlock.

264
00:15:39,105 --> 00:15:41,572
Uh, we're defending,
uh, Jennifer Holtz,

265
00:15:41,641 --> 00:15:43,752
uh, for the murder
of, uh... Dick Blake.

266
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:45,176
Uh, uh, Dick Blake.

267
00:15:45,244 --> 00:15:48,046
What do you mean?

268
00:15:48,114 --> 00:15:49,558
Jennifer's been arrested?

269
00:15:49,582 --> 00:15:50,982
Oh, this is a disaster.

270
00:15:51,050 --> 00:15:52,617
Uh, well,

271
00:15:52,685 --> 00:15:54,318
could we ask you
a few questions?

272
00:15:54,387 --> 00:15:55,897
I'm sorry. I-I... I can't.

273
00:15:55,921 --> 00:15:57,833
Uh, Cyril, just please
tell them anything

274
00:15:57,857 --> 00:15:58,968
that they want to know.

275
00:15:58,992 --> 00:16:00,352
Oh... Iris!

276
00:16:04,764 --> 00:16:06,742
None of this surprises me.

277
00:16:06,766 --> 00:16:08,977
Everyone knew Dick
and Jennifer were lovers.

278
00:16:09,001 --> 00:16:11,513
He was a rat with women.

279
00:16:11,537 --> 00:16:14,097
She was a jealous,
lovesick girl.

280
00:16:16,843 --> 00:16:19,476
And Spaulding Kane
is a spiteful phony

281
00:16:19,545 --> 00:16:21,745
who's thrilled to have
Jennifer out of the way.

282
00:16:24,150 --> 00:16:26,550
Hmm. And, so, uh,

283
00:16:26,619 --> 00:16:30,020
Jennifer, uh, Holtz
is the real thing, huh?

284
00:16:30,089 --> 00:16:31,989
Certainly.

285
00:16:34,060 --> 00:16:37,561
Even the best psychics
have a 75% accuracy rate.

286
00:16:37,630 --> 00:16:40,230
But take a look at this
chart I did on Jennifer

287
00:16:40,299 --> 00:16:42,859
for an article in<i> Cosmic
Consciousness Journal.</i>

288
00:16:42,902 --> 00:16:46,937
Jennifer Holtz is 96% accurate.

289
00:16:47,006 --> 00:16:48,805
Hmm.

290
00:16:48,874 --> 00:16:51,275
How often does she
predict things, like, um,

291
00:16:51,344 --> 00:16:54,111
it'll be hot in Atlanta in July?

292
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:55,480
You're a skeptic.

293
00:16:55,548 --> 00:16:57,348
That's fine.

294
00:16:57,417 --> 00:16:59,150
But believe it or not,

295
00:16:59,219 --> 00:17:01,452
there is a new
consciousness coming.

296
00:17:01,521 --> 00:17:04,889
And from the size of
this convention, a lot

297
00:17:04,957 --> 00:17:06,123
of money.

298
00:17:06,192 --> 00:17:09,093
That's what attracts
the frauds and the fakes.

299
00:17:11,431 --> 00:17:13,275
This is Marie's showroom.

300
00:17:13,299 --> 00:17:14,398
Huh.

301
00:17:14,467 --> 00:17:16,078
She works with
very powerful crystals

302
00:17:16,102 --> 00:17:18,869
used to induce channeling
and promote good health.

303
00:17:18,938 --> 00:17:21,271
Oh. Yeah.

304
00:17:21,340 --> 00:17:24,007
Promote good health, huh?

305
00:17:24,077 --> 00:17:25,609
Good health.

306
00:17:25,678 --> 00:17:26,777
Hmm.

307
00:17:28,013 --> 00:17:30,681
Didn't do much for his, did it?

308
00:17:30,750 --> 00:17:31,916
Huh.

309
00:17:31,985 --> 00:17:34,084
Oh, he's facing out here.

310
00:17:36,489 --> 00:17:39,923
That way... Hmm.

311
00:17:39,993 --> 00:17:42,793
Boy, he could have donated
a lot of blood, couldn't he?

312
00:17:42,862 --> 00:17:44,006
Yes.

313
00:17:44,030 --> 00:17:45,762
Hmm. What time
did the coroner say?

314
00:17:45,831 --> 00:17:47,776
Oh, about 9:00 p.m. About 9:00.

315
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:50,935
Murder weapon was a crystal
wand about 18 inches long.

316
00:17:51,003 --> 00:17:52,169
Those there.

317
00:17:52,238 --> 00:17:54,104
Marie designs those herself.

318
00:17:57,043 --> 00:17:59,677
Nothing's missing.

319
00:17:59,745 --> 00:18:01,579
Yeah.

320
00:18:01,648 --> 00:18:03,280
Good health.

321
00:18:03,349 --> 00:18:04,849
Good health.

322
00:18:09,421 --> 00:18:12,422
Uh, where would we
find Marie Willis now?

323
00:18:12,491 --> 00:18:14,558
Oh, she's probably
up in her room.

324
00:18:14,627 --> 00:18:16,527
She's upset about Jennifer,

325
00:18:16,595 --> 00:18:18,629
but she took Dick's
death hard, too.

326
00:18:18,698 --> 00:18:19,864
She loved him.

327
00:18:19,932 --> 00:18:21,365
He treated her very badly.

328
00:18:21,433 --> 00:18:24,568
But then, he treated
all women badly.

329
00:18:24,637 --> 00:18:26,937
You didn't like him
very much, did you?

330
00:18:27,006 --> 00:18:29,006
I hated him.

331
00:18:29,075 --> 00:18:32,242
He was a self-serving,
muscle-bound hustler.

332
00:18:32,311 --> 00:18:34,311
He was even taking
bribes from vendors

333
00:18:34,346 --> 00:18:36,158
for better positions
in the convention hall.

334
00:18:36,182 --> 00:18:39,016
Oh.

335
00:18:39,085 --> 00:18:42,587
Well, the murder
took place about 9:00.

336
00:18:42,655 --> 00:18:44,855
At 9:00, I was
having dinner with Iris

337
00:18:44,924 --> 00:18:46,891
in the hotel dining room.

338
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:48,693
Sorry.

339
00:18:48,761 --> 00:18:50,739
<i>But all those we've talked to,</i>

340
00:18:50,763 --> 00:18:52,162
all of 'em sounded

341
00:18:52,231 --> 00:18:53,709
like they wouldn't
mind killing, uh...

342
00:18:53,733 --> 00:18:54,877
Dick Blake. Yeah.

343
00:18:54,901 --> 00:18:56,500
Well, maybe Marie
will have a kind word

344
00:18:56,569 --> 00:18:57,668
to say about him.

345
00:18:57,737 --> 00:18:59,036
Yeah. Here.

346
00:18:59,105 --> 00:19:00,282
Hmm.

347
00:19:01,407 --> 00:19:02,685
I smell smoke.

348
00:19:02,709 --> 00:19:04,341
Yeah, it's in here.

349
00:19:04,410 --> 00:19:06,521
Hurry!

350
00:19:06,545 --> 00:19:07,957
There may be a
fire in here. Fire.

351
00:19:07,981 --> 00:19:10,147
A key. Key. Key.

352
00:19:10,216 --> 00:19:11,415
Oh. Oh, there.

353
00:19:11,484 --> 00:19:13,350
Come on. Come on.

354
00:19:29,401 --> 00:19:32,169
I should know better.

355
00:19:32,238 --> 00:19:35,939
Uh, well, yes, you're right.

356
00:19:36,008 --> 00:19:38,108
Suicide's no answer.

357
00:19:38,177 --> 00:19:40,110
Yes, it is.

358
00:19:41,281 --> 00:19:43,714
But it's very bad karma.

359
00:19:43,783 --> 00:19:47,351
Oh, well, whatever you say.

360
00:19:47,420 --> 00:19:51,088
Uh, do you... do you feel like
answering a few questions?

361
00:19:51,157 --> 00:19:53,724
I think so.

362
00:19:53,793 --> 00:20:00,163
Okay. Uh... This crystal wand...

363
00:20:05,137 --> 00:20:07,337
It's mine.

364
00:20:07,407 --> 00:20:08,639
I design them.

365
00:20:08,708 --> 00:20:09,852
Uh-huh.

366
00:20:09,876 --> 00:20:13,077
W-Was it missing
from your display case?

367
00:20:13,146 --> 00:20:16,046
I gave it to Dick a month ago.

368
00:20:18,117 --> 00:20:19,983
As a birthday present.

369
00:20:20,052 --> 00:20:21,418
Uh-huh.

370
00:20:21,487 --> 00:20:24,955
Oh, what was he doing in
the Crystal Suite that night?

371
00:20:25,024 --> 00:20:27,524
Had you arranged
to-to... to meet him there?

372
00:20:27,593 --> 00:20:29,526
No.

373
00:20:31,030 --> 00:20:33,564
I waited in my
room for him to call.

374
00:20:35,134 --> 00:20:36,733
I waited all night.

375
00:20:36,802 --> 00:20:38,835
You did?

376
00:20:38,904 --> 00:20:40,838
Yes.

377
00:20:42,975 --> 00:20:44,935
I would have done
anything for him.

378
00:20:46,012 --> 00:20:48,545
He lied to me.

379
00:20:48,614 --> 00:20:50,313
He cheated on me.

380
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:55,085
But I loved him.

381
00:20:55,154 --> 00:21:01,425
Mr. Matlock... I
had... I had no choice.

382
00:21:01,493 --> 00:21:04,395
You-You didn't kill him.

383
00:21:04,464 --> 00:21:06,063
No.

384
00:21:06,132 --> 00:21:07,431
He was my soul mate.

385
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:10,867
Uh... You say he cheated on you?

386
00:21:11,970 --> 00:21:14,004
He was a womanizer.

387
00:21:14,072 --> 00:21:18,242
Who-Who was he, uh, uh... with?

388
00:21:18,311 --> 00:21:20,277
I never dared meditate on that.

389
00:21:21,747 --> 00:21:23,814
I started working with crystals

390
00:21:23,882 --> 00:21:27,284
because I'm a very good psychic.

391
00:21:27,353 --> 00:21:29,653
But I... I can't bear

392
00:21:29,722 --> 00:21:33,023
to tell people the bad things
that I see in their future,

393
00:21:33,092 --> 00:21:35,893
or look at the bad things
that'll happen to me.

394
00:21:35,962 --> 00:21:39,263
Please don't ask me to
meditate on that. Please.

395
00:21:39,332 --> 00:21:40,730
I don't want to.

396
00:21:40,799 --> 00:21:44,835
No. No, I... No, I wouldn't
ask you to meditate on that.

397
00:21:44,904 --> 00:21:46,115
No.

398
00:21:46,139 --> 00:21:48,383
Who-Who was the last,

399
00:21:48,407 --> 00:21:52,543
uh, okay... woman
you saw him with?

400
00:21:54,380 --> 00:21:56,313
Jennifer.

401
00:21:57,483 --> 00:21:59,984
He said some very
sweet things to her.

402
00:22:00,052 --> 00:22:01,719
He even kissed her.

403
00:22:01,788 --> 00:22:08,025
For a moment... Mr. Matlock,

404
00:22:08,094 --> 00:22:10,628
Jennifer's my best friend,

405
00:22:10,696 --> 00:22:16,734
and she knew how
desperately I loved Dick.

406
00:22:18,170 --> 00:22:22,840
How desperately I loved him.

407
00:22:22,909 --> 00:22:25,175
She would never betray me.

408
00:22:25,244 --> 00:22:29,746
She would never, never...

409
00:22:34,954 --> 00:22:37,721
Good news from my spirit guides.

410
00:22:37,790 --> 00:22:39,367
You're going to
prove me innocent.

411
00:22:39,391 --> 00:22:41,258
Oh.

412
00:22:41,326 --> 00:22:44,328
Well, I might as
well just go fishing

413
00:22:44,397 --> 00:22:47,097
and let your spirit
guides take over.

414
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:49,480
Jennifer...

415
00:22:51,470 --> 00:22:54,604
we have a dirt poor case,

416
00:22:54,673 --> 00:22:58,676
and unless I can get
some hard, provable facts,

417
00:22:58,744 --> 00:23:03,013
you're going to be
convicted of murder.

418
00:23:03,082 --> 00:23:05,327
I don't know who's
trying to frame you,

419
00:23:05,351 --> 00:23:07,985
but whoever it is is
doing a pretty good job.

420
00:23:08,054 --> 00:23:10,321
But who would want to frame me?

421
00:23:10,389 --> 00:23:11,522
I don't know.

422
00:23:11,591 --> 00:23:12,989
Maybe Marie.

423
00:23:13,058 --> 00:23:15,859
She was damn
jealous of her soul mate,

424
00:23:15,928 --> 00:23:17,961
and he was coming on to you.

425
00:23:18,030 --> 00:23:20,631
Oh, Marie wouldn't, couldn't.

426
00:23:20,699 --> 00:23:23,867
But she's the best, most
honest person I know.

427
00:23:23,936 --> 00:23:27,671
Besides, everyone,
including Marie,

428
00:23:27,739 --> 00:23:30,974
knew that I had a reading
for Mrs. Murphy that night.

429
00:23:31,043 --> 00:23:34,044
I cancelled it at
the very last minute.

430
00:23:34,113 --> 00:23:36,846
Nobody knew I was meeting Dick.

431
00:23:36,915 --> 00:23:38,882
So no one's framing me.

432
00:23:39,952 --> 00:23:40,962
Hi, gang!

433
00:23:40,986 --> 00:23:43,254
Oh. Hi, Les.

434
00:23:43,322 --> 00:23:44,621
Hi, Ben.

435
00:23:44,690 --> 00:23:46,023
Hi, Jennifer.

436
00:23:46,092 --> 00:23:49,226
Well, I'm here for the
latest bulletin from beyond.

437
00:23:50,896 --> 00:23:54,931
Mr. Calhoun, could we
talk in private... later?

438
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:57,434
Oh, I got no secrets from Ben.

439
00:23:57,502 --> 00:23:58,782
We're buddies.

440
00:23:58,838 --> 00:24:01,171
Besides, I want to
show the skeptic here

441
00:24:01,240 --> 00:24:02,840
how you do your stuff.

442
00:24:06,845 --> 00:24:10,046
I want you to remember
that... Cosmically speaking...

443
00:24:10,115 --> 00:24:12,216
There are no accidents.

444
00:24:12,284 --> 00:24:13,783
You've lived many lives

445
00:24:13,852 --> 00:24:16,152
and will continue
to live many more.

446
00:24:16,222 --> 00:24:19,089
You're going to tell me who
I'm going to be born as next,

447
00:24:19,158 --> 00:24:21,078
so I can leave my
money to myself.

448
00:24:21,994 --> 00:24:23,160
Uh, no.

449
00:24:24,263 --> 00:24:26,196
The stock market's going down?

450
00:24:26,265 --> 00:24:27,431
No.

451
00:24:27,500 --> 00:24:30,033
I mean, yes, but you won't care.

452
00:24:30,102 --> 00:24:31,569
Oh, Mr. Calhoun.

453
00:24:31,637 --> 00:24:32,936
I'm obligated to tell you

454
00:24:33,005 --> 00:24:35,506
what my spirit
guides have told me.

455
00:24:35,575 --> 00:24:37,741
You won't live to
hear the verdict

456
00:24:37,810 --> 00:24:39,175
of this trial.

457
00:24:40,779 --> 00:24:42,813
Are you sure?

458
00:24:42,882 --> 00:24:44,114
I mean, I know

459
00:24:44,183 --> 00:24:46,183
your spirit guides
mean well, but...

460
00:24:46,252 --> 00:24:50,087
uh, maybe they're talking
about another Les Calhoun.

461
00:24:50,156 --> 00:24:52,222
Did they mention a ZIP code?

462
00:24:52,291 --> 00:24:55,592
Uh... I don't want to die.

463
00:25:04,536 --> 00:25:05,936
How's Marie?

464
00:25:06,005 --> 00:25:07,005
She'll be okay.

465
00:25:07,039 --> 00:25:08,371
Good.

466
00:25:08,440 --> 00:25:10,318
I got some stuff on Dick Blake.

467
00:25:10,342 --> 00:25:12,153
Yeah? Everything
from petty theft

468
00:25:12,177 --> 00:25:14,656
to major cons to kiting checks.

469
00:25:14,680 --> 00:25:15,812
No kidding.

470
00:25:15,881 --> 00:25:18,115
I wonder why Iris hired him.

471
00:25:18,183 --> 00:25:19,460
Maybe she didn't know.

472
00:25:19,484 --> 00:25:22,285
And he had other talents.

473
00:25:22,354 --> 00:25:23,486
Oh, yeah.

474
00:25:23,555 --> 00:25:24,655
I've been hearing that.

475
00:25:24,723 --> 00:25:25,800
Yeah. Yeah.

476
00:25:25,824 --> 00:25:27,035
He was a bodybuilder.

477
00:25:27,059 --> 00:25:28,059
Yeah, yeah.

478
00:25:28,127 --> 00:25:30,360
He spent part of the
time building his body

479
00:25:30,428 --> 00:25:32,763
and then the rest of it
chasing somebody else's.

480
00:25:32,831 --> 00:25:34,397
Well, they say it's
good for the heart.

481
00:25:34,466 --> 00:25:36,667
Yeah, I guess so.

482
00:25:36,735 --> 00:25:38,346
I did some poking around.

483
00:25:38,370 --> 00:25:40,370
Yeah? Look at this.

484
00:25:40,438 --> 00:25:42,305
Room service receipts

485
00:25:42,374 --> 00:25:44,786
from the week before the murder.

486
00:25:44,810 --> 00:25:46,376
All signed by him?

487
00:25:46,444 --> 00:25:47,377
Uh-huh.

488
00:25:47,445 --> 00:25:50,446
Look at the room number: 1737.

489
00:25:50,515 --> 00:25:53,116
Dick Blake was in room 247.

490
00:25:53,185 --> 00:25:55,185
Oh.

491
00:25:55,253 --> 00:25:59,022
Maybe you better
see who's in 1737.

492
00:25:59,091 --> 00:26:01,291
I'll hang around out here.

493
00:26:11,603 --> 00:26:13,882
Miss Vogel, you mind if I
ask you a few questions?

494
00:26:13,906 --> 00:26:14,838
I'm very busy.

495
00:26:14,907 --> 00:26:16,173
I understand.

496
00:26:16,242 --> 00:26:18,122
You'd rather I
ask them in court?

497
00:26:19,612 --> 00:26:21,278
Come in.

498
00:26:23,049 --> 00:26:25,393
What was your
relationship to Dick Blake?

499
00:26:25,417 --> 00:26:26,650
Strictly business.

500
00:26:26,719 --> 00:26:28,664
He managed the
day-to-day business

501
00:26:28,688 --> 00:26:30,265
of setting up the
convention for you?

502
00:26:30,289 --> 00:26:32,623
Yes, he did...
and none too well.

503
00:26:32,692 --> 00:26:35,826
Well, you couldn't have been
<i>too</i> unhappy with his work.

504
00:26:35,895 --> 00:26:40,097
Uh, champagne and
chocolate mousse at 2:00 a.m.

505
00:26:40,165 --> 00:26:42,032
Seems almost romantic.

506
00:26:43,502 --> 00:26:45,468
Dick's idea of a coffee break.

507
00:26:45,538 --> 00:26:47,737
That was the night
that we worked

508
00:26:47,806 --> 00:26:49,406
on the final convention budget.

509
00:26:49,475 --> 00:26:50,807
It took until dawn.

510
00:26:50,876 --> 00:26:53,510
Saving expenses was
not his strong point.

511
00:26:53,579 --> 00:26:55,846
Then, he wasn't...
living with you?

512
00:26:58,083 --> 00:26:59,849
No.

513
00:26:59,918 --> 00:27:03,153
No, Dick appealed to women
who needed to suffer for love.

514
00:27:03,221 --> 00:27:04,321
I'm not one of them.

515
00:27:08,326 --> 00:27:10,593
Thank you, Miss Vogel.

516
00:27:19,104 --> 00:27:20,970
Oh, hi, Les.

517
00:27:22,074 --> 00:27:23,206
Ben!

518
00:27:23,275 --> 00:27:24,607
Ben, I feel awful.

519
00:27:24,676 --> 00:27:26,043
How do I look?

520
00:27:26,111 --> 00:27:28,845
You're not going to
die. But she said I was.

521
00:27:28,914 --> 00:27:31,754
Well, she could
be wrong. Well...

522
00:27:32,217 --> 00:27:34,451
But you know what?

523
00:27:34,520 --> 00:27:38,688
I believe your
hair<i> is</i> growing in.

524
00:27:38,757 --> 00:27:40,591
Really? Uh-huh.

525
00:27:40,659 --> 00:27:41,939
Yeah.

526
00:27:45,965 --> 00:27:47,631
Ben.

527
00:27:47,699 --> 00:27:48,932
He wasn't living here,

528
00:27:49,001 --> 00:27:50,901
and none of his
things are in his room.

529
00:27:50,970 --> 00:27:53,170
You'd think a guy who
was working out all the time

530
00:27:53,239 --> 00:27:55,039
and chasing women
would want to take a shower.

531
00:27:55,107 --> 00:27:57,007
Yeah.

532
00:27:57,076 --> 00:27:59,187
Hey, who's the one person

533
00:27:59,211 --> 00:28:01,656
would do anything
Dick Blake said

534
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:04,581
without asking questions?

535
00:28:04,650 --> 00:28:06,349
Yeah.

536
00:28:06,418 --> 00:28:08,551
Call Marie.

537
00:28:11,557 --> 00:28:13,457
Okay, she said to
look in the closet.

538
00:28:13,525 --> 00:28:15,359
Uh-huh.

539
00:28:17,529 --> 00:28:20,130
Oh, here, here, here, here.

540
00:28:20,198 --> 00:28:22,644
Yeah, here's...
here's Dicky's bag.

541
00:28:22,668 --> 00:28:24,079
Poor Marie. Yeah, well,

542
00:28:24,103 --> 00:28:26,136
like you say, love is blind.

543
00:28:30,542 --> 00:28:31,741
Pay dirt.

544
00:28:31,810 --> 00:28:33,021
Huh.

545
00:28:33,045 --> 00:28:35,456
And everything he needed
to leave town in a hurry.

546
00:28:35,480 --> 00:28:37,247
Yeah.

547
00:28:37,316 --> 00:28:39,349
Yeah.

548
00:28:40,652 --> 00:28:43,053
There must be thousands.

549
00:28:43,122 --> 00:28:45,355
I think maybe we
better call the police.

550
00:28:48,460 --> 00:28:51,228
The state calls
Mr. Benjamin Matlock.

551
00:28:52,464 --> 00:28:53,797
Uh, Your Honor,

552
00:28:53,866 --> 00:28:57,367
I trust that my learned
colleague knows

553
00:28:57,436 --> 00:28:59,447
that an attorney
cannot be compelled

554
00:28:59,471 --> 00:29:01,616
to divulge privileged
information.

555
00:29:01,640 --> 00:29:04,007
I do not wish
privileged information,

556
00:29:04,075 --> 00:29:06,743
Your Honor, but if
my learned colleague

557
00:29:06,812 --> 00:29:08,879
is still unwilling to testify,

558
00:29:08,947 --> 00:29:12,049
I'm sure we can
corroborate the information

559
00:29:12,117 --> 00:29:14,084
from another witness.

560
00:29:23,963 --> 00:29:26,997
Mr. Matlock, do you
recall where you were

561
00:29:27,066 --> 00:29:29,377
and what you were doing
the night of the murder?

562
00:29:29,401 --> 00:29:33,203
I was having dinner with
you at Ray Templin's bar.

563
00:29:33,272 --> 00:29:36,039
And do you recall
our conversation

564
00:29:36,108 --> 00:29:37,473
about a young woman

565
00:29:37,542 --> 00:29:39,420
who made a certain prediction?

566
00:29:39,444 --> 00:29:40,743
Yes, I do.

567
00:29:40,812 --> 00:29:44,047
A prediction... and I quote...

568
00:29:44,115 --> 00:29:47,384
"within 48 hours, a
man would be murdered,

569
00:29:47,452 --> 00:29:50,420
stabbed in the back with
a glass spear"... unquote.

570
00:29:50,489 --> 00:29:53,356
Now, Mr. Matlock, wasn't
that prediction made

571
00:29:53,425 --> 00:29:55,191
a day<i> before</i> the murder?

572
00:29:55,260 --> 00:29:56,927
Uh, Your Honor, I object.

573
00:29:56,995 --> 00:29:59,329
Madam Prosecutor and I
were talking in a restaurant,

574
00:29:59,397 --> 00:30:01,357
and my testimony
should be stricken

575
00:30:01,399 --> 00:30:02,910
as hearsay and irrelevant.

576
00:30:02,934 --> 00:30:04,267
Objection overruled.

577
00:30:04,336 --> 00:30:05,502
Answer the question.

578
00:30:05,571 --> 00:30:07,070
Yes.

579
00:30:08,607 --> 00:30:09,887
Mr. Matlock,

580
00:30:09,941 --> 00:30:12,742
do you agree that
this crystal wand,

581
00:30:12,811 --> 00:30:14,344
which is the murder weapon,

582
00:30:14,413 --> 00:30:17,780
might be described
as a glass spear?

583
00:30:18,884 --> 00:30:20,083
I guess it might.

584
00:30:20,152 --> 00:30:21,152
Uh-huh.

585
00:30:21,220 --> 00:30:22,952
Now, Mr. Matlock,

586
00:30:23,021 --> 00:30:25,199
isn't it true that the person

587
00:30:25,223 --> 00:30:27,602
who made that
extraordinary prediction

588
00:30:27,626 --> 00:30:28,959
is your client,

589
00:30:29,028 --> 00:30:31,028
the defendant, Jennifer Holtz?

590
00:30:31,096 --> 00:30:32,328
Yes.

591
00:30:33,431 --> 00:30:37,067
I have just one more question.

592
00:30:37,136 --> 00:30:40,470
Do you think your client
can predict the future?

593
00:30:40,539 --> 00:30:41,872
Objection.

594
00:30:41,940 --> 00:30:44,374
This calls for a conclusion
on the part of the witness.

595
00:30:44,442 --> 00:30:47,002
I withdraw the question.

596
00:30:49,414 --> 00:30:51,848
Miss Vogel, this key ring,

597
00:30:51,917 --> 00:30:53,116
which you have identified

598
00:30:53,185 --> 00:30:55,251
as belonging to the
victim, Mr. Blake,

599
00:30:55,320 --> 00:30:58,221
contains keys to all
of the hotel suites,

600
00:30:58,290 --> 00:30:59,556
does it not?

601
00:30:59,625 --> 00:31:02,659
All of the suites that we
rented for our convention, yes.

602
00:31:02,728 --> 00:31:04,848
Dick... Mr. Blake... Was
my assistant manager.

603
00:31:05,764 --> 00:31:08,131
So, Mr. Blake could have entered

604
00:31:08,200 --> 00:31:12,569
any of the hotel suites to
meet anybody at any time,

605
00:31:12,637 --> 00:31:13,637
day or night?

606
00:31:13,672 --> 00:31:14,938
Yes, of course.

607
00:31:16,408 --> 00:31:18,976
Do you know who he
arranged to meet that night?

608
00:31:19,044 --> 00:31:20,044
No.

609
00:31:20,112 --> 00:31:21,711
He had his own life.

610
00:31:21,780 --> 00:31:25,315
Did Mr. Blake ever
describe to you

611
00:31:25,384 --> 00:31:26,928
his relationship
with the defendant,

612
00:31:26,952 --> 00:31:28,818
Jennifer Holtz?

613
00:31:29,921 --> 00:31:31,054
Yes.

614
00:31:31,122 --> 00:31:33,456
He told me that Jennifer
was crazy about him,

615
00:31:33,525 --> 00:31:35,503
called him night and day.

616
00:31:35,527 --> 00:31:37,226
I wasn't surprised.

617
00:31:37,295 --> 00:31:39,930
Dick seemed to attract
young, foolish girls.

618
00:31:39,998 --> 00:31:40,931
Object.

619
00:31:40,999 --> 00:31:42,099
Move to strike.

620
00:31:42,167 --> 00:31:43,567
Strike the last remark.

621
00:31:43,635 --> 00:31:45,235
No further questions.

622
00:31:46,772 --> 00:31:49,139
Considering the hour,
I'm going to recess

623
00:31:49,207 --> 00:31:51,174
until 9:00 a.m.
tomorrow morning.

624
00:31:56,414 --> 00:31:59,850
Uh... Ben?

625
00:31:59,918 --> 00:32:03,486
Uh, uh... uh, just curious.

626
00:32:03,555 --> 00:32:07,658
How much longer do
you think this trial will last?

627
00:32:07,726 --> 00:32:09,259
Well...

628
00:32:09,327 --> 00:32:12,462
I think it will last
long enough that...

629
00:32:12,531 --> 00:32:15,932
when you die, you'll
have a full head of hair.

630
00:32:26,145 --> 00:32:27,888
<i>I don't see what the point is.</i>

631
00:32:27,912 --> 00:32:30,013
I already told the
police what I saw.

632
00:32:30,081 --> 00:32:31,359
That woman ran out of here

633
00:32:31,383 --> 00:32:33,943
like demons were after her.

634
00:32:35,053 --> 00:32:36,486
Nothing's been touched.

635
00:32:36,555 --> 00:32:37,587
Court order.

636
00:32:37,656 --> 00:32:39,033
Court order... yeah, yeah, yeah.

637
00:32:44,062 --> 00:32:46,663
Well, he must have
been facing this way,

638
00:32:46,732 --> 00:32:47,932
'cause that's the way he fell.

639
00:32:47,966 --> 00:32:50,199
Yeah.

640
00:32:50,269 --> 00:32:54,604
Marie said that, uh,
she gave him that wand.

641
00:32:54,673 --> 00:32:57,574
And... maybe he brought
it up here with him?

642
00:32:57,643 --> 00:33:00,154
Why would he bring the
murder weapon with him?

643
00:33:00,178 --> 00:33:02,312
Well, surely, he
didn't bring it with him

644
00:33:02,381 --> 00:33:04,213
'cause he thought
somebody would kill him.

645
00:33:04,283 --> 00:33:07,317
Maybe he... maybe
he was going to sell it.

646
00:33:07,386 --> 00:33:08,851
Here, you take the wand.

647
00:33:08,920 --> 00:33:10,086
Slip up behind me.

648
00:33:10,155 --> 00:33:11,755
Okay. See if you can kill me.

649
00:33:13,224 --> 00:33:15,592
Okay. No, no, no, no.

650
00:33:15,661 --> 00:33:16,837
Not unless he was asleep.

651
00:33:16,861 --> 00:33:18,072
He would have seen his killer.

652
00:33:18,096 --> 00:33:19,274
I can see you.

653
00:33:19,298 --> 00:33:20,578
That's strange.

654
00:33:20,632 --> 00:33:25,402
Just... Doesn't make any sense.

655
00:33:36,248 --> 00:33:38,047
I'm dogged.

656
00:33:44,156 --> 00:33:47,924
Miss Willis, uh, how... how long

657
00:33:47,993 --> 00:33:51,127
have you known Jennifer Holtz?

658
00:33:51,196 --> 00:33:53,597
About seven years. And-and

659
00:33:53,665 --> 00:33:56,932
how would you describe
your relationship?

660
00:33:58,036 --> 00:33:59,102
We're friends.

661
00:33:59,171 --> 00:34:03,106
And you would never
do anything to hurt her,

662
00:34:03,175 --> 00:34:04,175
would you?

663
00:34:04,242 --> 00:34:05,308
Never.

664
00:34:06,578 --> 00:34:09,746
And she would never
do anything to hurt you.

665
00:34:09,815 --> 00:34:11,415
No, she wouldn't.

666
00:34:14,853 --> 00:34:17,788
I... I have a friend like that.

667
00:34:17,856 --> 00:34:20,724
His name is Lee Greenway.

668
00:34:20,793 --> 00:34:22,592
We've been friends for...

669
00:34:22,661 --> 00:34:24,428
oh, years and years and years.

670
00:34:24,496 --> 00:34:27,697
We grew up together,
and we never...

671
00:34:27,766 --> 00:34:30,300
never had a harsh
word between us.

672
00:34:30,368 --> 00:34:32,168
We never...

673
00:34:32,237 --> 00:34:34,437
never got mad and threw
rocks at one another,

674
00:34:34,506 --> 00:34:36,706
you know, the way boys will do.

675
00:34:36,775 --> 00:34:40,043
We were from the
country, I'm proud to say.

676
00:34:40,112 --> 00:34:43,146
And there was a
girl that Lee liked.

677
00:34:43,215 --> 00:34:44,480
Beautiful girl.

678
00:34:44,549 --> 00:34:49,685
She was tall, had
long black hair.

679
00:34:49,754 --> 00:34:51,587
And when Lee would see her,

680
00:34:51,656 --> 00:34:54,724
he had a little
poem he liked to say.

681
00:34:54,793 --> 00:34:58,361
He'd say, "If I'd
a-seed you a-coming,

682
00:34:58,430 --> 00:35:00,096
"I'd have knowed what to do.

683
00:35:00,165 --> 00:35:01,097
"I'd a-ris'

684
00:35:01,166 --> 00:35:04,100
both arms and a-wove at you."

685
00:35:04,169 --> 00:35:07,070
And she would laugh.

686
00:35:07,138 --> 00:35:11,942
And after while...
I started to say it...

687
00:35:12,010 --> 00:35:14,744
'cause I liked her myself.

688
00:35:16,581 --> 00:35:21,384
And Lee never got mad at me,

689
00:35:21,452 --> 00:35:24,554
because we were friends.

690
00:35:24,623 --> 00:35:29,091
And so, I think I understand
your friendship with Jennifer.

691
00:35:29,160 --> 00:35:32,395
You're like... two
halves of a coin.

692
00:35:32,463 --> 00:35:34,564
That's exactly the way we are.

693
00:35:34,633 --> 00:35:39,368
We're... twin souls
through many lives.

694
00:35:39,437 --> 00:35:40,770
Yeah.

695
00:35:43,308 --> 00:35:45,575
Were you aware or...

696
00:35:45,643 --> 00:35:48,278
or.. or were you ever suspicious

697
00:35:48,347 --> 00:35:52,382
of a relationship between
Jennifer and Dick Blake?

698
00:35:52,450 --> 00:35:55,184
Jennifer was counseling Dick.

699
00:35:56,287 --> 00:35:57,954
I see... I see.

700
00:35:58,023 --> 00:36:02,959
Even though... he
called and begged her

701
00:36:03,028 --> 00:36:06,329
to meet him secretly
late that night?

702
00:36:06,398 --> 00:36:08,798
That was for counseling
and nothing more?

703
00:36:08,867 --> 00:36:10,800
That's right.

704
00:36:10,868 --> 00:36:13,236
I would've known if
it was anything else.

705
00:36:13,305 --> 00:36:14,704
How would you have known?

706
00:36:14,773 --> 00:36:16,239
Jennifer would've told me.

707
00:36:16,308 --> 00:36:19,409
Even though she knew
how jealous you were of him?

708
00:36:19,478 --> 00:36:20,776
Yes.

709
00:36:20,845 --> 00:36:23,779
Jennifer told me everything.

710
00:36:23,848 --> 00:36:26,282
You were that close?

711
00:36:26,351 --> 00:36:28,284
Yes.

712
00:36:32,391 --> 00:36:34,324
I believe you are.

713
00:36:35,827 --> 00:36:37,760
I believe you are.

714
00:36:40,165 --> 00:36:45,468
And I believe that if
Jennifer had a vision,

715
00:36:45,537 --> 00:36:52,475
a vision... as
important... as death...

716
00:36:52,543 --> 00:36:55,478
Murder death...

717
00:36:55,546 --> 00:37:01,016
if she told anyone,
she would've told you.

718
00:37:01,086 --> 00:37:04,687
And I believe she
told you of her vision.

719
00:37:04,755 --> 00:37:07,690
And then when Dick
Blake was killed...

720
00:37:08,960 --> 00:37:11,294
you were terrified,

721
00:37:11,363 --> 00:37:13,329
that Jennifer had done it.

722
00:37:13,398 --> 00:37:16,333
And Jennifer knowing
of your jealousy

723
00:37:16,401 --> 00:37:21,871
was very frightened,
that you had done it.

724
00:37:21,940 --> 00:37:25,641
You have been
protecting each other.

725
00:37:31,616 --> 00:37:37,554
Jennifer... did tell you...

726
00:37:37,622 --> 00:37:40,223
every detail of her
prediction, didn't she?

727
00:37:44,162 --> 00:37:46,129
Yes.

728
00:37:47,231 --> 00:37:53,302
Now... this question
is very important

729
00:37:53,371 --> 00:37:59,141
and you must answer
it truthfully, at all costs.

730
00:38:00,244 --> 00:38:02,178
You did tell someone else

731
00:38:02,246 --> 00:38:08,184
about Jennifer's
prediction, didn't you?

732
00:38:15,860 --> 00:38:17,794
Yes.

733
00:38:23,501 --> 00:38:29,239
Mr. Henning, Miss
Willis did tell you

734
00:38:29,307 --> 00:38:32,275
about Jennifer's
prediction, didn't she?

735
00:38:32,343 --> 00:38:33,943
Yes.

736
00:38:34,012 --> 00:38:36,946
And I was convinced
it would come true.

737
00:38:37,015 --> 00:38:39,783
I've been observing
Jennifer for a long time.

738
00:38:39,851 --> 00:38:42,986
And I believe her
powers are extraordinary.

739
00:38:44,089 --> 00:38:49,025
Now, uh, on the
night of the murder,

740
00:38:49,094 --> 00:38:52,028
you were having
dinner with Miss Vogel.

741
00:38:52,097 --> 00:38:56,599
In fact, you used to have dinner
with Miss Vogel all the time.

742
00:38:56,668 --> 00:38:59,035
Yes, I did.

743
00:38:59,104 --> 00:39:05,641
Because there was a relationship
that ended around the first

744
00:39:05,710 --> 00:39:07,209
of the year.

745
00:39:07,278 --> 00:39:08,311
That's right.

746
00:39:08,379 --> 00:39:13,249
Now, as I said earlier,
we have a witness

747
00:39:13,318 --> 00:39:17,086
who saw Miss Vogel leave
the restaurant before 9:00.

748
00:39:17,155 --> 00:39:19,088
That same witness saw you

749
00:39:19,157 --> 00:39:22,091
leave the restaurant
before 9:00.

750
00:39:22,160 --> 00:39:23,259
Where did you go?

751
00:39:23,328 --> 00:39:24,493
To my room.

752
00:39:24,562 --> 00:39:25,761
Your Honor,

753
00:39:25,830 --> 00:39:29,398
the witness is not on
trial here. Uh, Your Honor,

754
00:39:29,467 --> 00:39:31,201
may I just continue with this?

755
00:39:31,269 --> 00:39:32,435
Proceed.

756
00:39:32,504 --> 00:39:33,703
Thank you.

757
00:39:33,771 --> 00:39:35,705
So you went to your room.

758
00:39:35,773 --> 00:39:38,708
Uh, did anyone visit you?

759
00:39:38,776 --> 00:39:40,543
No.

760
00:39:40,612 --> 00:39:43,546
So you were there all night?

761
00:39:43,615 --> 00:39:45,593
Yes. Alone?

762
00:39:45,617 --> 00:39:46,882
Yes!

763
00:39:46,951 --> 00:39:49,886
Let the record state

764
00:39:49,955 --> 00:39:53,389
that I'm showing the
witness State's Exhibit five.

765
00:39:53,458 --> 00:39:54,724
The scene of the murder...

766
00:39:54,793 --> 00:39:57,727
Better known to you
as the Crystal Suite.

767
00:39:57,796 --> 00:39:59,729
Now, as you can see,

768
00:39:59,798 --> 00:40:02,732
the victim's body
is facing this way.

769
00:40:02,801 --> 00:40:05,735
Facing the mirror.

770
00:40:05,804 --> 00:40:10,907
Now, how do you suppose
someone snuck up behind him

771
00:40:10,975 --> 00:40:13,909
and stabbed without
being seen in the mirror.

772
00:40:13,978 --> 00:40:16,379
I haven't the faintest idea.

773
00:40:16,448 --> 00:40:20,383
No? I mean, seems to me
a man the size of Dick Blake

774
00:40:20,452 --> 00:40:22,430
would've seen somebody
coming up to stab him,

775
00:40:22,454 --> 00:40:23,886
and put up a fight.

776
00:40:25,991 --> 00:40:27,156
One would think so.

777
00:40:27,225 --> 00:40:28,758
Yeah, one would.

778
00:40:28,826 --> 00:40:31,761
So...

779
00:40:31,829 --> 00:40:37,767
it brought to my mind
another possibility.

780
00:40:37,835 --> 00:40:40,770
Maybe...

781
00:40:40,838 --> 00:40:46,276
maybe Dick Blake wasn't
killed in the Crystal Suite.

782
00:40:46,344 --> 00:40:50,280
Maybe he was killed
somewhere else,

783
00:40:50,348 --> 00:40:52,282
and then his body was moved.

784
00:40:52,350 --> 00:40:53,682
What do you think?

785
00:40:54,786 --> 00:40:57,053
I suppose that's possible.

786
00:40:57,121 --> 00:40:59,088
Count on it.

787
00:40:59,157 --> 00:41:02,091
Count on it, Mr. Henning.

788
00:41:04,162 --> 00:41:06,930
I'm not psychic.

789
00:41:06,998 --> 00:41:08,932
I can't talk to the spirits.

790
00:41:11,069 --> 00:41:14,838
And even I know Dick Blake

791
00:41:14,906 --> 00:41:16,538
was killed in your room.

792
00:41:16,607 --> 00:41:17,673
Objection!

793
00:41:17,742 --> 00:41:19,587
Mr. Matlock, unless
you have some basis

794
00:41:19,611 --> 00:41:21,577
and proof, you'll
have to drop this

795
00:41:21,646 --> 00:41:24,206
immediately. I believe
I have it, Your Honor.

796
00:41:24,983 --> 00:41:26,961
Very well.

797
00:41:26,985 --> 00:41:30,086
Now-now-now... now
just-just... Just listen to this.

798
00:41:30,154 --> 00:41:32,088
See what you think.

799
00:41:35,760 --> 00:41:38,728
You stabbed Dick Blake

800
00:41:38,797 --> 00:41:40,729
with this crystal wand.

801
00:41:40,798 --> 00:41:43,132
And he fell on the rug

802
00:41:43,201 --> 00:41:46,169
in your room, bleeding heavily.

803
00:41:46,237 --> 00:41:49,672
And you drug Dick Blake...

804
00:41:51,042 --> 00:41:54,477
and the rug across the hall

805
00:41:54,546 --> 00:41:57,480
to the Crystal Suite.

806
00:41:57,549 --> 00:42:01,317
Where the body was found
just like Jennifer predicted.

807
00:42:01,386 --> 00:42:06,189
Then you brought the
rug from the Crystal Suite

808
00:42:06,257 --> 00:42:09,225
to your room.

809
00:42:09,294 --> 00:42:11,260
That's what caught ya.

810
00:42:11,329 --> 00:42:16,766
See, you thought
that all the rugs

811
00:42:16,834 --> 00:42:19,768
in all the suites,
in all the rooms

812
00:42:19,837 --> 00:42:22,771
were all alike.

813
00:42:24,175 --> 00:42:27,609
But they're not. Thank you.

814
00:42:27,678 --> 00:42:31,113
This is the rug from
the Crystal Suite.

815
00:42:31,182 --> 00:42:34,216
This rug...

816
00:42:34,285 --> 00:42:39,255
was impounded by
the police last night,

817
00:42:39,323 --> 00:42:43,026
for evidence from your room.

818
00:42:43,094 --> 00:42:48,264
Now, on the surface
these rugs look identical.

819
00:42:49,333 --> 00:42:51,267
And they are except...

820
00:42:52,971 --> 00:42:56,105
if you turn underneath
there's an inventory number

821
00:42:56,174 --> 00:42:59,108
from the hotel that
matches the room

822
00:42:59,176 --> 00:43:00,910
the rug goes in.

823
00:43:02,480 --> 00:43:04,091
This is the rug from
the Crystal Suite.

824
00:43:04,115 --> 00:43:05,125
The one with the blood.

825
00:43:05,149 --> 00:43:07,083
The one...

826
00:43:07,151 --> 00:43:10,086
Dick Blake fell on
after he was stabbed.

827
00:43:11,656 --> 00:43:17,593
And the number
on the rug is 122.

828
00:43:19,263 --> 00:43:22,698
Mr. Henning, what's
your room number?

829
00:43:22,767 --> 00:43:25,702
What's your room number?

830
00:43:29,240 --> 00:43:31,173
122.

831
00:43:33,278 --> 00:43:36,212
The rug the police impounded...

832
00:43:39,150 --> 00:43:44,353
has the number 123.

833
00:43:47,425 --> 00:43:52,361
That's the number...
of the Crystal room.

834
00:43:53,764 --> 00:43:55,364
And it came out of your room.

835
00:43:55,433 --> 00:43:57,032
You switched them, didn't you?

836
00:43:57,101 --> 00:43:59,035
Yes!

837
00:44:00,972 --> 00:44:03,605
But I never intended that...

838
00:44:03,674 --> 00:44:06,775
Jennifer would be
accused of Blake's murder.

839
00:44:08,847 --> 00:44:11,781
I believe you.

840
00:44:11,850 --> 00:44:14,784
And that's-that's what threw me.

841
00:44:16,488 --> 00:44:20,289
You never tried
to frame Jennifer.

842
00:44:20,358 --> 00:44:23,792
You thought she
had a perfect alibi.

843
00:44:27,399 --> 00:44:30,333
She had a reading that night...

844
00:44:31,836 --> 00:44:33,769
with Mrs. Murphy.

845
00:44:33,838 --> 00:44:37,173
How could you know

846
00:44:37,241 --> 00:44:40,176
she had canceled that reading

847
00:44:40,244 --> 00:44:43,178
to meet with Dick Blake.

848
00:44:44,482 --> 00:44:47,116
You would never do
anything to harm her,

849
00:44:47,185 --> 00:44:49,118
would you? Of course not.

850
00:44:51,188 --> 00:44:54,123
Jennifer is a
light in the world.

851
00:44:54,192 --> 00:44:56,625
She's the most special
person I've ever known.

852
00:44:56,694 --> 00:44:59,006
She's gifted beyond Nostradamus,

853
00:44:59,030 --> 00:45:01,964
beyond Edgar Cayce, beyond...

854
00:45:06,203 --> 00:45:09,138
Dick Blake wanted to use her...

855
00:45:09,206 --> 00:45:11,573
Use her as a woman
for his pleasure,

856
00:45:11,643 --> 00:45:14,243
and as a psychic for his profit.

857
00:45:14,311 --> 00:45:17,246
He was a carnal man who
abused the spiritual gifts of others.

858
00:45:17,314 --> 00:45:21,149
He mocked everything
the New Age stands for.

859
00:45:24,989 --> 00:45:30,126
Dick Blake knew you
didn't like him, didn't he?

860
00:45:30,194 --> 00:45:31,360
I made no secret of it.

861
00:45:31,429 --> 00:45:32,728
Why'd he come to your room?

862
00:45:32,797 --> 00:45:34,731
Greed!

863
00:45:34,799 --> 00:45:36,799
His greed like his
ego had no limits.

864
00:45:36,835 --> 00:45:39,080
He wanted to sell me the
crystal wand Marie gave him

865
00:45:39,104 --> 00:45:41,664
and other valuable
crystals I'm certain he stole.

866
00:45:43,608 --> 00:45:46,843
He brought the weapon with him.

867
00:45:46,911 --> 00:45:50,212
You see, it was meant to be.

868
00:45:52,350 --> 00:45:55,784
Oh, so, so you killed him...

869
00:45:57,855 --> 00:46:00,789
and moved his body,

870
00:46:00,858 --> 00:46:05,361
so it would look like
Jennifer's prediction

871
00:46:05,429 --> 00:46:07,196
had come true.

872
00:46:07,265 --> 00:46:09,631
The prediction did come true.

873
00:46:09,700 --> 00:46:11,667
I was only the means.

874
00:46:11,736 --> 00:46:15,171
I was destined
to kill Dick Blake

875
00:46:15,239 --> 00:46:17,907
just as Jennifer was
destined to reveal it.

876
00:46:17,975 --> 00:46:20,876
I knew the moment Marie told me,

877
00:46:20,945 --> 00:46:22,878
that vision was meant for me.

878
00:46:33,958 --> 00:46:38,861
Your Honor... I move to dismiss.

879
00:46:38,929 --> 00:46:41,096
Does prosecution
have any objection?

880
00:46:41,166 --> 00:46:43,632
None, Your Honor.

881
00:46:43,701 --> 00:46:46,135
Motion is granted.

882
00:46:46,203 --> 00:46:48,581
Miss Holtz, you're free to go.

883
00:46:48,605 --> 00:46:50,539
This court is adjourned.

884
00:46:53,511 --> 00:46:56,479
You'll be blessed with
long life and good health.

885
00:46:56,547 --> 00:46:58,480
But what about me?

886
00:46:58,549 --> 00:47:01,484
Les, the case was dismissed.

887
00:47:01,552 --> 00:47:03,151
There was no verdict.

888
00:47:03,220 --> 00:47:05,031
There was no jury
to give a verdict.

889
00:47:05,055 --> 00:47:06,622
There never will be.

890
00:47:06,691 --> 00:47:09,357
Then I'm gonna live!

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
